{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1859","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1859","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1859\",\"parent_revision\":\"b9af5569b9328dae6f6910b37a1f05a54ed3e4a4536fa21ed4d0b6dad2b64102\",\"root_revision\":\"b9af5569b9328dae6f6910b37a1f05a54ed3e4a4536fa21ed4d0b6dad2b64102\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-21)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Long-running plans were all-or-nothing. This blocks safe use of `implement-feature` for high-stakes features where users need to review intermediate output before irreversible downstream waves execute.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Users who want intermediate review gates on long plans; previously forced to choose between full autonomy and manual session termination.\\n- Bottleneck: The `implement-feature` Progress Loop is the central dispatch mechanism for all SAM execution \u2014 every feature implementation flows through it.\\n- Downstream: `complete-implementation`, `work-milestone`, and any skill invoking `implement-feature` inherits the mode behavior.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Users can review foundational wave output before triggering dependent implementation waves, reducing rework cost on architectural errors.\\n- `full_auto` default preserves backward compatibility \u2014 existing plans without an `autonomy` field continue to run without change.\\n- `checkpoint` adds safety for wave-level review without serializing individual task dispatch.\\n- `per_task` enables high-control workflows for sensitive or uncertain task sequences.\\n- Commit ownership policy correctly gates batch commits on `full_auto`/`checkpoint` and per-task commits on `per_task`.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `Plan.autonomy` is set:\\n\\n- `full_auto` (default): waves dispatch without interruption. Batch commits issued after step 5. No confirmation gates fire.\\n- `checkpoint`: all ready tasks in a wave dispatch in parallel via `TeamCreate`. After the wave completes and tasks remain, a wave-completion summary is displayed and explicit user confirmation is required before the next `sam_plan(action='ready')` call. Batch commits issued after step 5.\\n- `per_task`: ready tasks dispatched one at a time via single `Agent` calls (no `TeamCreate`). After each task completes (steps 4\u20134b), a compact result summary is displayed and explicit user confirmation is required before the next task dispatches. Per-task commits issued after step 4b.\\n\\n`sam_plan(action='status')` output includes an `autonomy` key with value matching the plan's configured mode. Pre-existing plans without the field return `\\\"full_auto\\\"`.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nAll target surfaces confirmed present:\\n\\n- `Plan.autonomy: Literal[\\\"full_auto\\\", \\\"checkpoint\\\", \\\"per_task\\\"] = Field(default=\\\"full_auto\\\", ...)` in `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` (lines 332\u2013334).\\n- `_sam_plan_status()` in `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` reads `Plan.autonomy` via `backend.read_plan()` and includes it in the returned dict (lines 412\u2013427).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` Progress Loop branches on `autonomy_mode` at step 3 (per_task serial path), step 4b commit ownership, Per-task Confirmation Gate (lines 248\u2013266), and Wave-Completion Confirmation Gate (lines 272+).\\n- Tests in `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` lines 724\u2013826.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `sam_plan(action='status', plan='P{N}')` output contains key `autonomy` with value matching the plan's configured mode. \u2014 VERIFIED: `_sam_plan_status()` reads `plan_data.get(\\\"autonomy\\\", \\\"full_auto\\\")` (server.py line 426); test `test_sam_plan_status_includes_autonomy_key` asserts `data[\\\"autonomy\\\"] == \\\"checkpoint\\\"`.\\n2. A plan with `autonomy: full_auto` (or no `autonomy` field) executes all waves without pausing \u2014 behavior identical to the pre-feature state. \u2014 VERIFIED: `full_auto` path has no gate branch (SKILL.md lines 82\u201394 dispatch via TeamCreate with no gate); backward-compatible default confirmed by `test_sam_plan_status_autonomy_defaults_to_full_auto`.\\n3. A plan with `autonomy: per_task` and two ready tasks causes the implement-feature orchestrator to dispatch task 1 via single `Agent` call, report its result, and present a user-confirmation prompt before dispatching task 2. Prompt wording is implementation-defined. \u2014 VERIFIED: SKILL.md lines 74\u201379 dispatch one task at a time; Per-task Confirmation Gate (lines 248\u2013266) describes result summary + confirmation prompt.\\n4. A plan with `autonomy: checkpoint` dispatches all tasks in the first ready wave in parallel via `TeamCreate`, then displays a wave-completion summary and waits for user confirmation before querying the next batch. \u2014 VERIFIED: SKILL.md lines 82\u201394 use `TeamCreate` for `full_auto`/`checkpoint`; Wave-Completion Confirmation Gate (lines 272+) fires when `autonomy_mode == \\\"checkpoint\\\"`.\\n5. `Plan.model_validate({'feature': 'test', 'tasks': []})` succeeds without providing `autonomy` \u2014 backward compatibility. \u2014 VERIFIED: `test_plan_model_validate_without_autonomy_defaults_to_full_auto` (line 782) and Pydantic default confirmed.\\n6. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/` passes with no regressions in SAM MCP tests. \u2014 DERIVABLE: tests exist; run to confirm.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Primary file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 `Plan.autonomy` field (lines 332\u2013334) |\\n| Primary file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 `_sam_plan_status()` (lines 412\u2013427) |\\n| Primary file | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Progress Loop autonomy branches (lines 41\u201395, 226\u2013299) |\\n| Test suite | `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` \u2014 autonomy tests (lines 724\u2013826) |\\n| Test suite | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` \u2014 backend autonomy tests |\\n| Docs | `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 `autonomy` field reference |\\n| Docs | `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 `autonomy` field noted in Required Reading |\\n| Related backlog | #2106 \u2014 Surface auto-fix diffs for human approval in /complete-implementation (autonomy does not gate fix-loop commits within complete-implementation) |\\n| Related backlog | #2444 \u2014 Add plan-approval artifact gate to implement-feature |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 `Plan` model is self-contained; no in-flight blockers.\\n- Blocks: #2106 (complete-implementation auto-fix diff approval) references `Plan.autonomy` \u2014 this item must remain stable as that feature extends the autonomy semantics.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall-Medium \u2014 Implementation is complete. Two surfaces (model field + SKILL.md prose branches) plus tests. Estimated 0.5\u20131 day was accurate.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Artifact Classification\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Feature (cross-cutting schema + skill behavior change)\\n- Behavioral boundary: The `implement-feature` Progress Loop pause/continue decision after each task or wave; the `sam_plan(action='status')` MCP output shape.\\n- Domain-semantic evaluation target: An orchestrator reading `autonomy` from `sam_plan status` and dispatching tasks in the mode that matches the plan's configured value.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone \u2014 all questions resolved (2026-04-22); all implementation surfaces confirmed present.\\n\\n### Groomed (2026-04-21)\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-05T08:15:24.354338Z</sub>\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\nAll questions resolved (2026-04-22):\\n\\n- **Q1** \u2014 When `autonomy: per_task` is active and two tasks are simultaneously ready, should the orchestrator dispatch in sequence or treat the batch as one unit?\\n  **Answer (human)**: Not directly addressed \u2014 [AUTO] treating as option (a) serial dispatch: each ready task is dispatched individually with a confirmation gate after each. Rationale: consistent with the `per_task` name semantics.\\n\\n- **Q2** \u2014 Schema default alignment: item description says `checkpoint` but Desired Structure says `full_auto`. Which is authoritative?\\n  **Answer (human)**: `full_auto` is the schema default. Pydantic field default is `\\\"full_auto\\\"`. Existing plans without an `autonomy` field get `full_auto` behavior.\\n\\n- **Q3** \u2014 Is the confirmation prompt text `\\\"Confirm next task\\\"` a hard requirement (tested by transcript grep) or illustrative?\\n  **Answer (human)**: Illustrative. AC3 has been revised to remove the literal transcript grep test.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n- Goal: Add `Plan.autonomy` field (`full_auto`/`checkpoint`/`per_task`) to the SAM Plan model and gate the `implement-feature` Progress Loop on the configured mode, so users can choose between uninterrupted execution, wave-level confirmation gates, and per-task confirmation gates.\\n- Status: APPROVED\\n- AVAILABLE:\\n  - `Plan.autonomy: Literal[\\\"full_auto\\\", \\\"checkpoint\\\", \\\"per_task\\\"] = \\\"full_auto\\\"` field confirmed present at `models.py` lines 332\u2013334.\\n  - `_sam_plan_status()` in `server.py` (lines 412\u2013427) calls `backend.read_plan()` and merges `autonomy` key into the returned dict \u2014 same pattern as `_sam_plan_ready`.\\n  - `implement-feature/SKILL.md` Progress Loop (lines 41\u201395, 248\u2013299) branches on `autonomy_mode` for `per_task` serial dispatch, `checkpoint` wave-gate, and `full_auto` (no-gate) paths.\\n  - Commit Ownership section (lines 226\u2013244) correctly gates commit timing on `autonomy_mode`.\\n  - All three test cases (`test_sam_plan_status_includes_autonomy_key`, `test_sam_plan_status_autonomy_defaults_to_full_auto`, `test_plan_model_validate_without_autonomy_defaults_to_full_auto`) confirmed present in `tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` lines 724\u2013826.\\n  - `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` reference `autonomy` field.\\n  - All Q1\u2013Q3 human questions resolved (2026-04-22).\\n- DERIVABLE:\\n  - Test pattern for parametrized three-value validation derived from existing status tests \u2014 confirmed present as `test_plan_model_validate_accepts_all_three_autonomy_values` (lines 804\u2013826).\\n- MISSING: None.\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `sam_plan(action='status')` output contains key `autonomy`.\\n- With `autonomy: per_task` set on the plan and two ready tasks, implement-feature dispatches task 1, reports, and halts for user input before dispatching task 2 (verified by transcript showing the literal prompt string `\\\"Confirm next task\\\"`).\\n- Default behavior for existing plans (no `autonomy` field) matches today's `full_auto` execution \u2014 backward compatible.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add autonomy modes (full_auto/checkpoint/per_task) to implement-feature dispatch loop** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md \u2014 pattern: Parallel Execution with Configurable Autonomy (feature 3)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe Progress Loop in `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` (lines 34\u2013206) dispatches ready tasks in batches without user review between batches. There is no plan-level `autonomy` field on the `Plan` model, and no branch in the SKILL mermaid graph that inserts a user-confirmation gate between waves. The only checkpoint is the Completion Gate after **all** tasks finish \u2014 no intermediate wave-level or task-level gate exists.\\n\\nSymptom: long-running plans are all-or-nothing. A user who wants to review after a foundational wave before letting downstream waves run has no way to ask for that gate short of killing the session.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`Plan.autonomy: Literal[\\\"full_auto\\\", \\\"checkpoint\\\", \\\"per_task\\\"] = \\\"checkpoint\\\"` added to `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py`. `implement-feature/SKILL.md` grows an autonomy-gated branch in its Progress Loop: after each batch (checkpoint) or each task (per_task), the orchestrator reports a compact summary and waits for user confirmation before pulling the next batch. `full_auto` preserves today's behavior. Value readable via `sam_plan(action='status')`.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"bbd7061a8146d6f418e75d14bfca2a506ae24fd56faa89cb9a1ff3e63d1f3d30\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS-q1Q\"}"}